WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.118
Trace the liquid from the vessel through
the outlet and transfer hose.

2
00:00:04.238 --> 00:00:07.182
Include impeller surfaces, seals, gaskets

3
00:00:07.302 --> 00:00:09.831
and valve seats, not just the vessel
shell.

4
00:00:09.951 --> 00:00:12.980
The diagram marks these as one contact
path.

5
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.865
A statement that the vessel is stainless
steel leaves elastomers

6
00:00:16.985 --> 00:00:19.118
and purchased components unresolved.

7
00:00:19.238 --> 00:00:21.670
Ask how each material is identified

8
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.713
and justified for the product, cleaning
agents,

9
00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:28.716
temperature and contact time relevant to
the intended use.

10
00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:33.773
A material certificate can support
identity, but identity alone does

11
00:00:33.893 --> 00:00:38.458
not prove compatibility with a specific
formulation or cleaning regime.

12
00:00:38.578 --> 00:00:40.946
Similarly, a surface-finish number is

13
00:00:41.066 --> 00:00:43.882
useful only with a justified requirement

14
00:00:44.002 --> 00:00:46.264
and a defined verification method.

15
00:00:46.384 --> 00:00:48.389
This introductory module does

16
00:00:48.509 --> 00:00:51.026
not prescribe a universal steel grade,

17
00:00:51.146 --> 00:00:53.194
roughness value or elastomer.

18
00:00:53.314 --> 00:00:55.314
In the fictional review,

19
00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:58.250
mark the gasket compatibility statement
missing

20
00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:02.594
and request product-specific evidence from
the responsible specialists.

21
00:01:03.214 --> 00:01:05.732
The design sketch contrasts a clear outlet

22
00:01:05.852 --> 00:01:08.433
path with a pocket that may retain liquid.

23
00:01:08.553 --> 00:01:10.772
Review access, cleaning coverage,

24
00:01:10.892 --> 00:01:13.708
disassembly needs, drainage and
inspection.

25
00:01:13.828 --> 00:01:16.475
Consider whether maintenance can be
performed

26
00:01:16.595 --> 00:01:19.795
without creating an uncontrolled product-
quality risk.

27
00:01:19.915 --> 00:01:23.008
A favourable drawing is only a design
argument:

28
00:01:23.128 --> 00:01:27.416
cleaning effectiveness still needs the
applicable validation evidence.

29
00:01:27.536 --> 00:01:31.760
Do not copy a hygienic-design ratio from
another application

30
00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.059
and present it as a universal GMP rule.

31
00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:37.679
Our worked finding is specific:

32
00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:42.044
the outlet drawing shows a retained pocket
with no cleaning rationale.

33
00:01:42.164 --> 00:01:44.724
Record the drawing revision and location,

34
00:01:44.844 --> 00:01:49.111
request a revised arrangement or a
justified control strategy,

35
00:01:49.231 --> 00:01:51.231
and assign an owner.

36
00:01:51.351 --> 00:01:55.404
Link the response to installation
inspection and the cleaning study.

37
00:01:55.524 --> 00:01:58.852
Avoid a vague action such as improve
cleanability.

38
00:01:58.972 --> 00:02:03.900
A closed action needs reviewed evidence
that addresses the actual concern,

39
00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.410
not merely an email saying resolved.
